### Preprocessing

Run Length Encoding

```
O(n)
```

Build Gain Array

```
O(n)
```

Build Segment Tree

```
O(n)
```

Total preprocessing

```
O(n)
```

---

### Per Query

Binary Search

```
O(log n)
```

Segment Tree Query

```
O(log n)
```

Total

```
O(log n)
```

---

### Overall

```
O(n + q log n)
```

which easily passes the constraints (`n, q ≤ 10^5`).

---

# Space Complexity

Run-length encoded zero-block information:

```
O(number of zero blocks) ≤ O(n)
```

Gain array:

```
O(n)
```

Segment tree:

```
O(n)
```

Overall auxiliary space:

```
O(n)
```

This is the optimal approach for the given constraints, reducing the brute-force `O(nq)` solution to `O(n + q log n)` by preprocessing zero runs and answering each query with binary searches plus a segment-tree range-maximum query.
